A citation graph is an important part of modern scientometrics (the
field of analyzing and measuring of scientific literature).
To
construct it, we need to disambiguate citations: determine which paper
cites which paper.  While many publishers now deposit citation data in
a machine readable format, some do not\Dash and there are millions of
older papers where only textual citation strings are available.  Since
manual conversion of these strings to parsed entries is not possible,
we need to teach machines how to do this.

